-- title:
--   Height-one primes at the node admit centred ℚ̄-points
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}=\,$`AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$, a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$, an element $a \in k$, and an intermediate field $K$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ that is finite over $\mathbb{Q}$; write $A_0 = A \cap K$ for `coeffSubring A K` and let $\mathrm{red}_0$ be the restriction of $\mathrm{red}$ to $A_0$. Let $C$ denote `jIntegralClosure (1 * q) A K`: the subring of Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ consisting of those elements of the subfield generated by the constant series of $K$ together with $j =$ `jqModC` and $j_q =$ `jqNModC` of level $1 \cdot q$ that are integral over the subring generated by the constant series of $A_0$ and $j$. Let $\mathfrak{p} \subset C$ be a prime ideal of height $1$ with $(q : C) \notin \mathfrak{p}$, and assume that for every $s \in A_0[X_0,X_1]$ whose reduction $s^{\mathrm{red}_0}(a, a^q) \in k$ is nonzero, the series $s(j, j_q)$, whenever it lies in $C$, lies outside $\mathfrak{p}$. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\sigma : C \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ker \sigma = \mathfrak{p}$, with $\sigma$ sending the constant series of each $b \in A_0$ (when that series lies in $C$) to $b$, and such that if $j \in C$ then $\sigma(j) \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,\sigma(j) = a$, and if $j_q \in C$ then $\sigma(j_q) \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,\sigma(j_q) = a^q$.
--
--   This is the horizontal case of the classification of height-one primes on the normal affine model of $X_0(q)$ over $A \cap K$: a closed point $\mathfrak{p}$ whose pullback to $A_0[j, j_q]$ avoids the denominators at the node is realised by a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point whose coordinates are $A$-integral and reduce exactly to $(a, a^q)$. It is the commutative-algebra input to [`ModularCurve.exists_place_centred_node_of_height_one_of_natCast_notMem`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_place_centred_node_of_height_one_of_natCast_notMem), which converts such a homomorphism into a place of the function field centred at the node.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_NodeLocalized_exists_ringHom_ker_eq_centred_of_height_one_of_natCast_notMem.lean

